This screen is important because it is the Master Navigation and Risk Prioritisation Layer. It sits above individual simulations and directs the operator based on the current risk condition.
SEXTANT MASTER CONSOLE
Operational Manual Section — Master Risk Navigation Layer
1. Purpose
The Sextant Master Console is the central operational gateway that provides an overview of system condition and directs users toward appropriate operational modules.
Its purpose is to:
Present overall system risk status
Prioritise operational attention
Provide access to simulation and control environments
Support contingency planning and resilience analysis
2. Screen Components
🟠 WARNING
This indicates that the system has detected a condition requiring attention.
It does not necessarily mean system failure.
The warning state represents:
elevated stress
increased monitoring requirement
possible need for scenario analysis
Example status levels:
🟢 NORMAL — Stable operation
🟡 WATCH — Increased monitoring
🟠 WARNING — Elevated risk
🔴 CRITICAL — Immediate attention
Risk Score: 43
The Risk Score provides a simplified numerical representation of current simulated system pressure.
Purpose:
Allow quick operator understanding
Compare different scenarios
Support risk-based navigation
Example interpretation:
0–20    Stable
21–40   Watch
41–60   Warning
61–80   Severe
81–100  Critical
(Current example: 43 = Warning range)
3. Navigation Modules
Run Simulation Screen v2
Accesses the simulation execution environment.
Function:
Select scenarios
Run controlled stress tests
Observe RP-04 system response
Flow:
Scenario Input
       ↓
RP-04 Engine
       ↓
Simulation Output
       ↓
Risk Assessment
Industrial Control Screen v1
Provides an operational environment for industrial resilience scenarios.
Potential applications:
infrastructure systems
facility operations
critical equipment resilience
contingency planning
Schneider Datacentre Pilot
Provides a dedicated pilot scenario environment for data centre resilience assessment.
Focus areas:
operational continuity
infrastructure dependencies
fallback planning
system availability
4. Risk-Driven Navigation Layer
This is the key concept of this screen.
Instead of the operator searching through all modules, the system guides attention based on risk condition.
Concept:
System Condition
        ↓
Risk Score
        ↓
Priority Level
        ↓
Recommended Module
        ↓
Operational Response
5. Operational Role
The Master Console acts as the command layer:
Gateway Console
↓
Master Console
↓
Simulation / Industrial / Pilot Modules
↓

